#: ../../chapters/04-productivity/environmental-productivity-ml-common-reference.md:1
#: 24615fe9b3bf48e197c0a4b55deda5e0
msgid "Environmental Productivity over Time with Adjacent-Period ML"
msgstr "使用相邻期 ML 衡量跨期环境生产率"

#: ../../chapters/04-productivity/environmental-productivity-ml-common-reference.md:3
#: 1c489541d52d4439a0556250e99b4aac
msgid ""
"An electricity producer reports more power and less carbon dioxide than it "
"did last year. A water utility treats more water while discharging fewer "
"residuals. A farm raises marketable output while reducing nutrient loss. "
"Each sounds like an environmental productivity improvement, but none can be "
"assessed from the raw changes alone. Inputs may also have changed, the "
"attainable production--pollution trade-off may have improved, and each "
"annual plan must be assessed against the production and pollution-control "
"opportunities observed at both dates."
msgstr "一家发电企业报告其发电量高于上年而二氧化碳排放更少；供水企业处理更多水量却排放更少残余物；农场增加可销售产出并减少养分流失。这些现象听起来都像环境生产率改善，但仅凭原始变化无法判断。投入也可能发生变化，可实现的生产—污染权衡可能改善，而且必须把每年的完整方案分别放到两个日期观测到的生产与污染控制机会下评价。"

#: ../../chapters/04-productivity/environmental-productivity-ml-common-reference.md:11
#: a6e1c94a4d5743d48bbc955042004375
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"The Malmquist--Luenberger (ML) index organizes these issues within one model"
" of production and pollution. It treats desirable and undesirable outputs as"
" joint consequences of production and asks how an environmental improvement "
"programme changes over time {cite:p}`chung1997`. Its classic adjacent-period"
" formulation evaluates the two operating plans against both period-specific "
"technologies."
msgstr ""
"Malmquist--"
"Luenberger（ML）指数把这些问题组织到一个生产与污染联合模型中。它把合意产出和非合意产出视为生产的联合结果，并考察一套环境改进方案如何随时间变化"
" {cite:p}`chung1997`。经典相邻期形式把两个经营方案分别放到两个时期特定技术下评价。"

#: ../../chapters/04-productivity/environmental-productivity-ml-common-reference.md:17
#: 641484a8dd054d418957c3434d8d73f9
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"These are not ordinary productivity indexes with a pollution penalty "
"attached after estimation. The undesirable-output technology, the assumed "
"possibilities for pollution reduction, and the improvement programme all "
"determine what “environmental productivity” means. That is why the ML index "
"remains distinct from a conventional Malmquist index with a pollution column"
" appended after the fact {cite:p}`fare1994`."
msgstr ""
"这不是普通生产率指数估计完毕后再附加一项污染惩罚。非合意产出技术、污染削减可能性的假设以及改进方案共同决定“环境生产率”的含义。因此，ML "
"指数不同于事后向普通 Malmquist 指数增加一列污染数据 {cite:p}`fare1994`。"

#: ../../chapters/04-productivity/environmental-productivity-ml-common-reference.md:24
#: a64c05c1385b48febf1b74f091e0aa9f
msgid "The central questions are economic and managerial:"
msgstr "核心问题具有明确的经济与管理含义："

#: ../../chapters/04-productivity/environmental-productivity-ml-common-reference.md:26
#: a3ab28cc461a4279a62f2335d57cf211
msgid ""
"Has an organization reduced the environmental performance shortfall visible "
"in its own period?"
msgstr "组织是否缩小了本期可见的环境绩效缺口？"

#: ../../chapters/04-productivity/environmental-productivity-ml-common-reference.md:28
#: d1ae3f7dae28440a9aeac11514f0cc34
msgid ""
"Has the best-observed opportunity for producing useful output with fewer "
"undesirable consequences become more favorable?"
msgstr "以更少非合意后果生产有用产出的最佳观测机会是否变得更有利？"

#: ../../chapters/04-productivity/environmental-productivity-ml-common-reference.md:30
#: 75f65417e314439497a987a13aaafe1d
msgid ""
"Can both annual operating plans be supported by the opportunities observed "
"at the other date?"
msgstr "两个年度的经营方案能否分别由另一日期所观测到的生产与污染控制机会支持？"

#: ../../chapters/04-productivity/environmental-productivity-ml-common-reference.md:33
#: 8d279b99fdae4c519dee67fb55ff80f1
msgid ""
"The answers are conditional on the data and production assumptions. They "
"describe benchmark-relative change; identifying the effects of management, "
"investment, or regulation requires additional evidence."
msgstr "答案都以数据和生产假设为条件，描述的是相对标杆变化；识别管理、投资或监管的作用还需要额外证据。"

#: ../../chapters/04-productivity/environmental-productivity-ml-common-reference.md:37
#: c96276f9c02441cea8a5fe8c6ea48941
msgid ""
"Environmental productivity begins by modeling production and pollution "
"together"
msgstr "环境生产率始于对生产与污染的联合建模"

#: ../../chapters/04-productivity/environmental-productivity-ml-common-reference.md:39
#: ce974a97ac4d419a810157711ac232e4
msgid "Let an operating plan in period $\\sigma$ be"
msgstr "设时期 $\\sigma$ 的经营方案为"

#: ../../chapters/04-productivity/environmental-productivity-ml-common-reference.md:41
#: db105f1b1db74cab9f3f59f2b260cb0a
msgid ""
"\n"
"z^\\sigma=(x^\\sigma,y^\\sigma,b^\\sigma),\n"
msgstr ""
"\n"
"z^\\sigma=(x^\\sigma,y^\\sigma,b^\\sigma),\n"

#: ../../chapters/04-productivity/environmental-productivity-ml-common-reference.md:45
#: 2f2d97f7deb24f419d0991dc680a1d08
msgid ""
"where $x$ is a vector of inputs, $y$ a vector of desirable outputs, and $b$ "
"a vector of undesirable outputs. The period-$\\tau$ environmental technology"
" $\\mathcal T^\\tau$ contains the input--output--residual plans treated as "
"attainable by the observations admitted to reference period $\\tau$. Thus "
"$\\sigma$ identifies when the plant operated, whereas $\\tau$ identifies the"
" body of evidence used to judge that operation. The distinction matters "
"whenever one year's plan is appraised using another year's production and "
"pollution-control opportunities."
msgstr ""
"其中，$x$ 是投入向量，$y$ 是合意产出向量，$b$ 是非合意产出向量。时期 $\\tau$ 的环境技术 $\\mathcal T^\\tau$ "
"包含获准进入参照期 $\\tau$ 的观测所支持的可实现投入—产出—残余物方案。因此，$\\sigma$ 标识工厂实际经营的时期，$\\tau$ "
"标识用于评价该经营活动的证据集合。当某一年度方案使用另一年度的生产与污染控制机会评价时，这一区分至关重要。"

#: ../../chapters/04-productivity/environmental-productivity-ml-common-reference.md:53
#: fba553fc2ce94cbda9664b3a772a0162
msgid ""
"The label $b$ is not merely a minus sign attached to an ordinary output. The"
" technology must describe why the residual accompanies useful production and"
" under what conditions it can be reduced. Three choices are especially "
"important."
msgstr "标识 $b$ 不是简单给普通产出加上负号。技术必须说明为什么残余物伴随有用生产产生，以及在何种条件下能够减少。以下三项选择尤其重要。"

#: ../../chapters/04-productivity/environmental-productivity-ml-common-reference.md:57
#: c6a518515ddc478eb967a2045d1caf43
msgid ""
"First, desirable output and pollution are treated as **joint products**. In "
"the classic formulation, null jointness rules out positive desirable "
"production with no associated undesirable output. This prevents the frontier"
" from offering pollution- free production merely because zero emissions "
"would look preferable."
msgstr "第一，把合意产出与污染视为**联合产品**。在经典形式中，零结合性排除有正的合意生产却没有相应非合意产出的情形，从而避免仅仅因为零排放看起来更好，前沿就提供实际并不存在的无污染生产。"

#: ../../chapters/04-productivity/environmental-productivity-ml-common-reference.md:62
#: 436fcb14b6be4130a1def2f8ae16c9fb
msgid ""
"Second, undesirable outputs are **weakly disposable**. A producer cannot "
"freely delete pollution from an otherwise unchanged activity. Under the "
"common-factor representation used here, curtailing the joint activity "
"reduces desirable and undesirable outputs together. This encodes the idea "
"that pollution reduction is technologically costly unless a cleaner "
"production or abatement activity is actually observed in the data."
msgstr "第二，非合意产出具有**弱可处置性**。生产者不能在其他活动不变时免费删除污染。本章使用共同因子表示：联合活动收缩时，合意产出和非合意产出同时减少。这体现了污染削减在技术上有成本，除非数据中实际观测到更清洁的生产或治理活动。"

#: ../../chapters/04-productivity/environmental-productivity-ml-common-reference.md:69
#: c1cc90c0c3484225abdc6d6837180820
msgid ""
"Third, the analyst declares what one unit of environmental improvement "
"means. For the classic ML programme, inputs remain fixed, desirable outputs "
"expand in their observed proportions, and undesirable outputs contract in "
"their observed proportions. Starting from $(x,y,b)$, a programme of size "
"$\\beta$ requests"
msgstr ""
"第三，分析者声明一个单位的环境改善具体表示什么。在经典 ML 方案中，投入保持不变，合意产出按观测比例扩张，非合意产出按观测比例收缩。从 "
"$(x,y,b)$ 出发，规模为 $\\beta$ 的方案要求"

#: ../../chapters/04-productivity/environmental-productivity-ml-common-reference.md:74
#: 4e564fb85b9944588e081f80bdcda071
msgid ""
"\n"
"\\bigl(x,(1+\\beta)y,(1-\\beta)b\\bigr).\n"
msgstr ""
"\n"
"\\bigl(x,(1+\\beta)y,(1-\\beta)b\\bigr).\n"

#: ../../chapters/04-productivity/environmental-productivity-ml-common-reference.md:78
#: a933d6c18c0f4f77b0a927fd9ff76652
msgid ""
"For a plant, $\\beta=0.05$ therefore means a simultaneous 5 percent "
"expansion of each desirable output and a 5 percent contraction of each "
"undesirable output, without increasing the input vector. This is a demanding"
" joint performance programme. It is not equivalent to reducing emissions "
"intensity, reducing total emissions regardless of output, or attaching a "
"monetary damage value to pollution."
msgstr ""
"因此，对一家工厂而言，$\\beta=0.05$ 表示投入向量不增加时，每项合意产出同时扩张 5%，每项非合意产出同时收缩 "
"5%。这是一项要求严格的联合绩效方案，不等同于降低排放强度、不考虑产出而只减少总排放，也不等同于给污染附加货币损害价值。"

#: ../../chapters/04-productivity/environmental-productivity-ml-common-reference.md:84
#: e196770f2eed48638f5b0611ea7e737c
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"More generally, collect the nonnegative direction magnitudes for the "
"period-$\\sigma$ plan in $g^\\sigma=(0,g^{y,\\sigma},g^{b,\\sigma})$, where "
"the leading zero holds inputs fixed. Its directional appraisal against "
"reference technology $\\mathcal T^\\tau$ is"
msgstr ""
"更一般地，把时期 $\\sigma$ 方案的非负方向幅度写为 "
"$g^\\sigma=(0,g^{y,\\sigma},g^{b,\\sigma})$，开头的 0 表示投入不变。它相对于参照技术 $\\mathcal"
" T^\\tau$ 的方向性评价为"

#: ../../chapters/04-productivity/environmental-productivity-ml-common-reference.md:88
#: 50eb7319f2f146e7ba9bbd6955aae180
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"\n"
"D^\\tau(z^\\sigma;g^\\sigma)\n"
"=\\sup\\left\\{\\beta:\n"
"\\bigl(x^\\sigma,y^\\sigma+\\beta g^{y,\\sigma},\n"
"b^\\sigma-\\beta g^{b,\\sigma}\\bigr)\\in\\mathcal T^\\tau\n"
"\\right\\}.\n"
msgstr ""
"\n"
"D^\\tau(z^\\sigma;g^\\sigma)\n"
"=\\sup\\left\\{\\beta:\n"
"\\bigl(x^\\sigma,y^\\sigma+\\beta g^{y,\\sigma},\n"
"b^\\sigma-\\beta g^{b,\\sigma}\\bigr)\\in\\mathcal T^\\tau\n"
"\\right\\}.\n"

#: ../../chapters/04-productivity/environmental-productivity-ml-common-reference.md:96
#: be5e57c374c447d4be4a9cbbde53e263
msgid ""
"For a plan observed in period $\\sigma$, the classic observation-scaled "
"choice is $g^\\sigma=(0,y^\\sigma,b^\\sigma)$. DEAPack stores the desirable-"
" and undesirable-output components as nonnegative magnitudes; the "
"contraction of bad outputs is supplied by the model. Entering negative bad-"
"output directions would reverse that meaning a second time."
msgstr ""
"对时期 $\\sigma$ 观测到的方案，经典的观测尺度选择为 $g^\\sigma=(0,y^\\sigma,b^\\sigma)$。DEAPack "
"把合意与非合意产出方向分量存为非负幅度；非合意产出的收缩符号由模型提供。输入负的非合意产出方向会再次反转其含义。"

#: ../../chapters/04-productivity/environmental-productivity-ml-common-reference.md:102
#: eecf5b634f7847a1aac13eb09b77c5bb
msgid ""
"A positive distance says that some of the chosen improvement remains "
"attainable relative to the reference technology. A value near zero says that"
" the plan is already a benchmark for this programme. Neither statement "
"establishes efficiency under every possible mix change or every "
"environmental technology."
msgstr ""
"正的距离表示相对于参照技术，所选改进方案仍有一部分可以实现；接近 0 "
"表示该方案已是这套改进方案的标杆。两者都不能证明该方案在所有组合变化或所有环境技术下均有效率。"

#: ../../chapters/04-productivity/environmental-productivity-ml-common-reference.md:107
#: 2fb7886cb0cf464da0b77a61e5816cd6
msgid "Why the assumptions change the estimand"
msgstr "为什么假设会改变估计对象"

#: ../../chapters/04-productivity/environmental-productivity-ml-common-reference.md:109
#: 0cedc2d6e82d47a7a65bd3ddbca83871
msgid ""
"The classic ML formulation used here adopts a constant-returns-to-scale "
"(CRS), common-factor weak-disposal technology with null jointness and the "
"observation-scaled programme $(0,y,b)$. These choices give the index a "
"precise meaning:"
msgstr "本章经典 ML 形式采用规模报酬不变（CRS）、共同因子弱可处置技术、零结合性以及观测尺度方案 $(0,y,b)$。这些选择赋予指数明确含义："

#: ../../chapters/04-productivity/environmental-productivity-ml-common-reference.md
#: 980e5abf56d64c5181b417c8533ba252
msgid "Modeling choice"
msgstr "建模选择"

#: ../../chapters/04-productivity/environmental-productivity-ml-common-reference.md
#: a3c633b889544403a2963be84a2927a2
msgid "Meaning of the comparison"
msgstr "比较含义"

#: ../../chapters/04-productivity/environmental-productivity-ml-common-reference.md
#: d8fb448596634c2fb39521dec3bcad6a
msgid "Inputs held fixed"
msgstr "投入保持不变"

#: ../../chapters/04-productivity/environmental-productivity-ml-common-reference.md
#: 1a1937e6b6704ac8920d7ea83b0be0e6
msgid "Improvement is sought without expanding the stated resource commitment"
msgstr "在不扩大既定资源承诺的情况下寻求改进"

#: ../../chapters/04-productivity/environmental-productivity-ml-common-reference.md
#: 99e05ff9bb244cdcb4318fc8def88eb2
msgid "Desirable direction $g^y=y$"
msgstr "合意方向 $g^y=y$"

#: ../../chapters/04-productivity/environmental-productivity-ml-common-reference.md
#: 110d34babecb429a84d672fc96ce42fd
msgid "All desirable outputs expand in their observed proportions"
msgstr "全部合意产出按观测比例扩张"

#: ../../chapters/04-productivity/environmental-productivity-ml-common-reference.md
#: 718e3c8442be49bcb57fbac614107ad8
msgid "Undesirable direction $g^b=b$"
msgstr "非合意方向 $g^b=b$"

#: ../../chapters/04-productivity/environmental-productivity-ml-common-reference.md
#: 7cf4abb8ffc14035a13847fa7f0777fa
msgid "All undesirable outputs contract in their observed proportions"
msgstr "全部非合意产出按观测比例收缩"

#: ../../chapters/04-productivity/environmental-productivity-ml-common-reference.md
#: 7b84b8ced024422c9985bbe0beff75b5
msgid "Weak disposal and joint production"
msgstr "弱可处置性与联合生产"

#: ../../chapters/04-productivity/environmental-productivity-ml-common-reference.md
#: 76dea94c6cbb4511b9ebadc47b38d4c9
msgid "Pollution cannot be erased independently of observed production activity"
msgstr "污染不能独立于观测生产活动被删除"

#: ../../chapters/04-productivity/environmental-productivity-ml-common-reference.md
#: 0007b0066f244ee6b6b178759d582132
msgid "CRS"
msgstr "CRS"

#: ../../chapters/04-productivity/environmental-productivity-ml-common-reference.md
#: cade356dad8a4d89be52d948cd4c45b6
msgid ""
"Activities may be proportionally replicated; the index does not isolate "
"scale effects"
msgstr "活动可以同比例复制；指数不单独识别规模效应"

#: ../../chapters/04-productivity/environmental-productivity-ml-common-reference.md:121
#: dbd7e45c35294dea914950d57f1321a8
msgid ""
"Changing any row changes the question, not merely the numerical technique. "
"If a facility has a separately observed scrubber, recycling process, or "
"treatment stage, common-factor weak disposal may be too restrictive. If "
"physical material balance is central, a mass-conserving technology may be "
"needed. If reducing one pollutant while another increases is a realistic "
"programme, the proportional direction may be inappropriate. Those production"
" accounts belong in the environmental-efficiency analysis that precedes the "
"temporal index; they should not be selected after seeing which specification"
" gives a preferred trend."
msgstr "改变任一行都会改变研究问题，而不只是改变数值技术。如果设施另有观测到的洗涤、回收或处理阶段，共同因子弱可处置性可能过于严格；若物质平衡是核心，可能需要守恒质量的技术；若现实方案允许一种污染物减少而另一种增加，比例方向可能不适用。这些生产账户应在时间指数之前的环境效率分析中决定，不能看到哪种设定趋势更合意后再选择。"

#: ../../chapters/04-productivity/environmental-productivity-ml-common-reference.md:130
#: 077ab71c786842f485519813cbb74d52
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"The practical lesson is simple: define the pollution-generating process "
"before measuring its change. The chapter on {doc}`../03-environmental/06"
"-undesirable-outputs-ddf` develops the underlying technology choices in more"
" detail."
msgstr ""
"实践原则很简单：先定义污染生成过程，再度量其变化。{doc}`../03-environmental/06-undesirable-outputs-"
"ddf` 章节更详细地讨论底层技术选择。"

#: ../../chapters/04-productivity/environmental-productivity-ml-common-reference.md:135
#: f952e2a9b9db41feb7cc7c1f5d1ad12a
msgid "Adjacent-period ML uses four evaluations"
msgstr "相邻期 ML 使用四次评价"

#: ../../chapters/04-productivity/environmental-productivity-ml-common-reference.md:137
#: 481acbeb19a24e7f94d1e570bd2b79b6
msgid ""
"Suppose an organization is observed in adjacent periods $t$ and $t+1$. Write"
" $D_\\sigma^\\tau=D^\\tau(z^\\sigma;g^\\sigma)$ for the directional distance"
" of the plan observed in period $\\sigma$ when it is evaluated against the "
"technology supported by reference period $\\tau$. Four questions are "
"required:"
msgstr ""
"设同一组织在相邻时期 $t$ 和 $t+1$ 被观测。记 "
"$D_\\sigma^\\tau=D^\\tau(z^\\sigma;g^\\sigma)$，表示时期 $\\sigma$ 的方案相对于参照期 "
"$\\tau$ 所支持技术的方向性距离。需要回答四个问题："

#: ../../chapters/04-productivity/environmental-productivity-ml-common-reference.md
#: 2394d09a12044deda4a57673070f1b9e
msgid "Evaluation"
msgstr "评价"

#: ../../chapters/04-productivity/environmental-productivity-ml-common-reference.md
#: 632454353d0046ffb88986f1a7b60a01
msgid "Management question"
msgstr "管理问题"

#: ../../chapters/04-productivity/environmental-productivity-ml-common-reference.md
#: aceee54ee79a4152af4e352a03c59df2
msgid "$D_t^t$"
msgstr "$D_t^t$"

#: ../../chapters/04-productivity/environmental-productivity-ml-common-reference.md
#: 399a9989f9fb4190ba15a1a37c1b59b9
msgid ""
"How much of the old plan's improvement programme remains attainable under "
"old-period opportunities?"
msgstr "在旧时期生产机会下，旧方案还有多少改进方案可以实现？"

#: ../../chapters/04-productivity/environmental-productivity-ml-common-reference.md
#: f30fb3de0b574b7697022473d61141f2
#, python-brace-format
msgid "$D_{t+1}^{t+1}$"
msgstr "$D_{t+1}^{t+1}$"

#: ../../chapters/04-productivity/environmental-productivity-ml-common-reference.md
#: 321b9e68bcc04202a040b01419edfad4
msgid "How much remains attainable for the new plan under new-period opportunities?"
msgstr "在新时期生产机会下，新方案还有多少改进方案可以实现？"

#: ../../chapters/04-productivity/environmental-productivity-ml-common-reference.md
#: 42728a03817f469596ecda0312ec874f
#, python-brace-format
msgid "$D_{t+1}^t$"
msgstr "$D_{t+1}^t$"

#: ../../chapters/04-productivity/environmental-productivity-ml-common-reference.md
#: 13a25d7d25e24c8cb0530eace7f8670d
msgid ""
"How would the new plan compare with the opportunities observed in the old "
"period?"
msgstr "新方案相对于旧时期观测生产机会有怎样的表现？"

#: ../../chapters/04-productivity/environmental-productivity-ml-common-reference.md
#: a81077fde2b6408c89b001c73837def7
#, python-brace-format
msgid "$D_t^{t+1}$"
msgstr "$D_t^{t+1}$"

#: ../../chapters/04-productivity/environmental-productivity-ml-common-reference.md
#: c3cb95c247a94f4f9e939ae90a4b86cb
msgid ""
"How would the old plan compare with the opportunities observed in the new "
"period?"
msgstr "旧方案相对于新时期观测生产机会有怎样的表现？"

#: ../../chapters/04-productivity/environmental-productivity-ml-common-reference.md:149
#: 97fdaeb1f7fa433eaa6d525c91c26da2
msgid ""
"The diagonal comparisons describe each plan relative to its contemporaneous "
"environment. The off-diagonal comparisons ask whether one period's operation"
" can be supported by the other period's production and emissions "
"opportunities."
msgstr "两个对角线比较描述每个方案相对于同期环境的表现；两个非对角线比较考察某一时期经营活动能否由另一时期的生产与排放机会支持。"

#: ../../chapters/04-productivity/environmental-productivity-ml-common-reference.md:153
#: 0cb4138ae8b1456c96ecd4aeb23c9687
msgid ""
"A two-by-two matrix crosses old and new operating plans with old and new "
"environmental production opportunities, producing two contemporaneous and "
"two cross-period evaluations"
msgstr "一个 2×2 矩阵把新旧经营方案与新旧环境生产机会交叉，形成两次同期评价和两次跨期评价"

#: ../../chapters/04-productivity/environmental-productivity-ml-common-reference.md:158
#: 339b694101124c14ae226ac9c7de7401
msgid ""
"The four evaluations behind adjacent-period ML. Using both period "
"technologies avoids making the measured transition depend solely on choosing"
" the old or the new benchmark."
msgstr "相邻期 ML 背后的四次评价。使用两个时期的技术，避免让测得转变完全取决于只选旧标杆或只选新标杆。"

#: ../../chapters/04-productivity/environmental-productivity-ml-common-reference.md:162
#: c0e5d3c6957c43f9b23edbe65f29572b
msgid "Two change ratios can be formed, one under each reference period:"
msgstr "可以在每个参照期下分别构造一个变化比率："

#: ../../chapters/04-productivity/environmental-productivity-ml-common-reference.md:164
#: ba52b3d349cd4fcc85e542a5ec58b44a
msgid ""
"\n"
"R^t\n"
"=\\frac{1+D_t^t}{1+D_{t+1}^t},\n"
"\\qquad\n"
"R^{t+1}\n"
"=\\frac{1+D_t^{t+1}}{1+D_{t+1}^{t+1}}.\n"
msgstr ""
"\n"
"R^t\n"
"=\\frac{1+D_t^t}{1+D_{t+1}^t},\n"
"\\qquad\n"
"R^{t+1}\n"
"=\\frac{1+D_t^{t+1}}{1+D_{t+1}^{t+1}}.\n"

#: ../../chapters/04-productivity/environmental-productivity-ml-common-reference.md:172
#: f3a01f0ba9cb40809f65286b268e33ad
msgid "The adjacent-period ML index takes their geometric mean:"
msgstr "相邻期 ML 指数取二者的几何平均："

#: ../../chapters/04-productivity/environmental-productivity-ml-common-reference.md:174
#: 768b4855f7a640d7a1f70d31d31da162
msgid ""
"\n"
"ML^{t,t+1}\n"
"=\\left[\n"
"\\frac{1+D_t^t}{1+D_{t+1}^t}\n"
"\\frac{1+D_t^{t+1}}{1+D_{t+1}^{t+1}}\n"
"\\right]^{1/2}.\n"
msgstr ""
"\n"
"ML^{t,t+1}\n"
"=\\left[\n"
"\\frac{1+D_t^t}{1+D_{t+1}^t}\n"
"\\frac{1+D_t^{t+1}}{1+D_{t+1}^{t+1}}\n"
"\\right]^{1/2}.\n"

#: ../../chapters/04-productivity/environmental-productivity-ml-common-reference.md:182
#: fff276a25de7417b8624b6e3489c74cc
msgid ""
"Under this convention, $ML>1$ denotes environmental productivity "
"improvement, $ML=1$ no measured change, and $ML<1$ decline. “Improvement” "
"means that the later plan performs better under the specified useful-output-"
"expansion and bad-output-contraction programme, averaged over the two "
"period-specific reference policies."
msgstr ""
"按本章约定，$ML>1$ 表示环境生产率改善，$ML=1$ 表示未测得变化，$ML<1$ "
"表示下降。“改善”是指后期方案在既定的有用产出扩张—非合意产出收缩方案下表现更好，并对两个时期特定参照政策取平均。"

#: ../../chapters/04-productivity/environmental-productivity-ml-common-reference.md:187
#: 43a4102cdeb04c8eb68c37d433c97a80
msgid ""
"The added 1 is part of the classic multiplicative construction. Because the "
"direction determines the units and scale of $D$, changing the improvement "
"programme can change the index. Direction choice is therefore an empirical "
"commitment, not a harmless normalization."
msgstr "加上的 1 是经典乘法构造的一部分。由于方向决定 $D$ 的单位和尺度，改变改进方案可能改变指数。因此，方向选择是一项实证承诺，而不是无关紧要的标准化。"

#: ../../chapters/04-productivity/environmental-productivity-ml-common-reference.md:192
#: e0f0a9a5332c44fea8f52a33a3f14802
msgid "Two change stories inside the ML index"
msgstr "ML 指数中的两个变化叙事"

#: ../../chapters/04-productivity/environmental-productivity-ml-common-reference.md:194
#: 1c19324a2fee4b4d89343e91113a35d4
msgid ""
"The index can be decomposed into a change in contemporaneous operating "
"performance and a change in best-observed production opportunity."
msgstr "该指数可分解为同期经营绩效变化与最佳观测生产机会变化。"

#: ../../chapters/04-productivity/environmental-productivity-ml-common-reference.md:197
#: 18db67a15b494c5ea270de7af6d6e4e0
msgid "The operating-performance component is"
msgstr "经营绩效分量为"

#: ../../chapters/04-productivity/environmental-productivity-ml-common-reference.md:199
#: 84eab20f1980404b8e099e89905209dc
msgid ""
"\n"
"EC_{ML}\n"
"=\\frac{1+D_t^t}{1+D_{t+1}^{t+1}}.\n"
msgstr ""
"\n"
"EC_{ML}\n"
"=\\frac{1+D_t^t}{1+D_{t+1}^{t+1}}.\n"

#: ../../chapters/04-productivity/environmental-productivity-ml-common-reference.md:204
#: 3574a4460cce41f0aa576bbce92ca33e
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"When $EC_{ML}>1$, the later operation leaves a smaller shortfall relative to"
" its own period's benchmark. When it is below one, the contemporaneous "
"shortfall has widened. This is often called efficiency change. In management"
" language, it records whether the organization realizes more or less of the "
"environmental production potential observed around it at each date."
msgstr ""
"$EC_{ML}>1$ 时，后期经营相对于自身时期标杆的缺口更小；低于 1 "
"时，同期缺口扩大。这通常称为技术效率变化。用管理语言说，它记录组织在各日期实现了周围所观测环境生产潜力的更多还是更少。"

#: ../../chapters/04-productivity/environmental-productivity-ml-common-reference.md:210
#: 2b6fd99d8e4045aa964cfb9340147fc7
msgid "The best-practice-opportunity component is"
msgstr "最佳实践机会分量为"

#: ../../chapters/04-productivity/environmental-productivity-ml-common-reference.md:212
#: 4a6e86ba82744a5eaa98d96dad9d38cc
msgid ""
"\n"
"TC_{ML}\n"
"=\\left[\n"
"\\frac{1+D_t^{t+1}}{1+D_t^t}\n"
"\\frac{1+D_{t+1}^{t+1}}{1+D_{t+1}^t}\n"
"\\right]^{1/2},\n"
msgstr ""
"\n"
"TC_{ML}\n"
"=\\left[\n"
"\\frac{1+D_t^{t+1}}{1+D_t^t}\n"
"\\frac{1+D_{t+1}^{t+1}}{1+D_{t+1}^t}\n"
"\\right]^{1/2},\n"

#: ../../chapters/04-productivity/environmental-productivity-ml-common-reference.md:220
#: 9e44ea25fe324580ace35b1334f062b1
msgid "with the exact identity"
msgstr "并满足精确恒等式"

#: ../../chapters/04-productivity/environmental-productivity-ml-common-reference.md:222
#: 7609c498a0a346daade609a1b8644046
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"\n"
"ML=EC_{ML}\\times TC_{ML}.\n"
msgstr ""
"\n"
"ML=EC_{ML}\\times TC_{ML}.\n"

#: ../../chapters/04-productivity/environmental-productivity-ml-common-reference.md:226
#: 67cc3d22dd3143fcba9a95fc0be6d083
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"$TC_{ML}>1$ means that the best-observed trade-off among inputs, desirable "
"outputs, and undesirable outputs became more favorable for the two plans "
"being compared. A value below one records a less favorable observed "
"opportunity. Although software often calls this technical change, it is "
"safer to report it as **best-practice-opportunity change**. The component "
"does not reveal why the benchmark changed."
msgstr ""
"$TC_{ML}>1$ 表示在所比较两个方案附近，投入、合意产出与非合意产出之间的最佳观测权衡变得更有利；低于 1 "
"表示观测机会变得更不利。软件通常把它称为技术变动，但报告时使用**最佳实践机会变化**更稳妥。该分量不能揭示标杆为什么改变。"

#: ../../chapters/04-productivity/environmental-productivity-ml-common-reference.md:233
#: 680da5ec27c74617b63f5849b273cb4b
msgid ""
"Two environmental productivity stories contrast an organization narrowing "
"its contemporaneous operating shortfall with a change in the best-observed "
"useful-output and undesirable-output opportunity"
msgstr "两个环境生产率叙事：组织缩小同期经营缺口，与最佳观测有用产出—非合意产出机会发生变化"

#: ../../chapters/04-productivity/environmental-productivity-ml-common-reference.md:238
#: 5d91de4f16d24a2caf4092f498fdcf97
msgid ""
"Environmental productivity can grow because an organization realizes more of"
" the opportunity observed in its period, because the best-observed "
"opportunity improves, or because both occur. It is an accounting description"
" rather than a causal allocation of responsibility."
msgstr "环境生产率可能因为组织更多地实现本期所观测机会、最佳观测机会改善，或二者同时发生而增长。这是会计描述，不是责任的因果分配。"

#: ../../chapters/04-productivity/environmental-productivity-ml-common-reference.md:244
#: 134699843864461c956973d3fe04e9ec
msgid ""
"The distinction matters for management. A narrowing contemporaneous "
"shortfall may be consistent with better maintenance, fuel management, "
"capacity use, or operating discipline. A favorable opportunity change may be"
" consistent with cleaner equipment, learning, altered production mix, or new"
" environmental practice among benchmark units. But the index does not "
"observe those mechanisms directly. Data revisions, weather, case mix, fuel "
"quality, regulation, and changes in measurement can produce similar "
"patterns."
msgstr "该区别对管理很重要。同期缺口缩小可能与维护、燃料管理、产能利用或经营纪律改善一致；有利的机会变化可能与更清洁设备、学习、生产组合调整或标杆单元采用新的环境实践一致。但指数不直接观测这些机制，数据修订、天气、业务组合、燃料质量、监管和测量变化都可能产生相似模式。"

#: ../../chapters/04-productivity/environmental-productivity-ml-common-reference.md:252
#: 3fa7c3a125484d3ab87174b53f172b83
msgid ""
"The two components can also move in opposite directions. A plant may improve"
" relative to its contemporaries while the system's best-observed opportunity"
" becomes less favorable, or lose relative ground while best practice "
"improves. Reporting only the headline ML value can hide that strategically "
"important difference."
msgstr "两个分量也可能反向移动。工厂可以在系统最佳观测机会变差时相对同业改善，也可以在最佳实践改善时相对落后。只报告 ML 核心值可能掩盖这一具有战略意义的差异。"

#: ../../chapters/04-productivity/environmental-productivity-ml-common-reference.md:257
#: 2ea37cb7656545d58ef4b5e3e6a59335
msgid "A signed cross-technology distance can carry economic information"
msgstr "带符号跨技术距离可以承载经济信息"

#: ../../chapters/04-productivity/environmental-productivity-ml-common-reference.md:259
#: d533f2f33fb34acc846ee656bde27247
msgid ""
"The evaluated plan is always included in its own-period technology in an "
"ordinary self-inclusive analysis, so a zero contemporaneous improvement is "
"feasible and the diagonal distance is nonnegative. A cross-period plan need "
"not belong to the other period's technology. Its optimal directional "
"distance can therefore be negative."
msgstr "在普通自包含分析中，被评价方案总是纳入自身时期技术，因此同期评价至少可以选择零改进，对角线距离非负。跨期方案则不一定属于另一时期技术，其最优方向性距离因而可能为负。"

#: ../../chapters/04-productivity/environmental-productivity-ml-common-reference.md:264
#: 9d96abb1d08242299aade57b97d3dd21
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"A negative $D_{t+1}^t$ says that the later plan is beyond what the old "
"technology can represent in the declared favorable programme. To make it "
"compatible with the old reference, the comparison would have to move in the "
"unfavorable direction—less desirable output, more undesirable output, or the"
" corresponding combination defined by the programme. This can be evidence of"
" a meaningful change in represented opportunity."
msgstr ""
"负的 $D_{t+1}^t$ "
"表示在既定有利改进方案下，后期方案超出了旧技术能够表示的范围。若要使其与旧参照兼容，比较必须向不利方向调整——减少合意产出、增加非合意产出，或按方案定义作相应组合。这可能是所代表生产机会发生实质变化的证据。"

#: ../../chapters/04-productivity/environmental-productivity-ml-common-reference.md:271
#: 0f1d15b37b5a4c6280ba58e0ed0cdb2f
msgid "Three empirical outcomes must remain separate:"
msgstr "必须区分三类实证结果："

#: ../../chapters/04-productivity/environmental-productivity-ml-common-reference.md:233
#: 07cfbf198a544f7e808a4bdafc6ab080
msgid "Outcome"
msgstr "结果"

#: ../../chapters/04-productivity/environmental-productivity-ml-common-reference.md:233
#: e62832223f5444d693b19a2e5d455e6c
msgid "Interpretation"
msgstr "解释"

#: ../../chapters/04-productivity/environmental-productivity-ml-common-reference.md:233
#: 827757e29a414ff780983d8deae26e71
msgid "Appropriate treatment"
msgstr "适当处理"

#: ../../chapters/04-productivity/environmental-productivity-ml-common-reference.md:233
#: d5a4b21fe2ff4dd084b63cef15096e01
msgid "A valid comparison gives $D<0$ and $1+D>0$"
msgstr "有效比较得到 $D<0$ 且 $1+D>0$"

#: ../../chapters/04-productivity/environmental-productivity-ml-common-reference.md:233
#: 16bdab77014b40ea9b17842a968cbf56
msgid "The plan lies beyond the other period's opportunity in the declared programme"
msgstr "方案在既定改进方向上超出另一时期生产机会"

#: ../../chapters/04-productivity/environmental-productivity-ml-common-reference.md:233
#: 9777b0991ad948769102a71bac4be3fd
msgid "Retain the signed distance in ML"
msgstr "在 ML 中保留带符号距离"

#: ../../chapters/04-productivity/environmental-productivity-ml-common-reference.md:233
#: 4b6cf3d2b26f405ebc3a2579ba5a9c33
msgid "No feasible comparison exists"
msgstr "不存在可行比较"

#: ../../chapters/04-productivity/environmental-productivity-ml-common-reference.md:233
#: 282fd17cae6b4731b24bfeb86d620348
msgid ""
"No admissible reference activity represents the plan under the maintained "
"environmental technology"
msgstr "在维持的环境技术下，没有合格参照活动能够表示该方案"

#: ../../chapters/04-productivity/environmental-productivity-ml-common-reference.md:233
#: d558c0cb19a342508eb9effb6e9fadd7
msgid "Leave the transition undefined and investigate the technology and data"
msgstr "把该转变保留为未定义，并检查技术和数据"

#: ../../chapters/04-productivity/environmental-productivity-ml-common-reference.md:233
#: 3771cdf289724c798ff46ff852504ff4
msgid "A valid comparison gives $1+D\\le0$"
msgstr "有效比较得到 $1+D\\le0$"

#: ../../chapters/04-productivity/environmental-productivity-ml-common-reference.md:233
#: d88041b1db644957935e03331714799d
msgid "The multiplicative factor needed by ML is not admissible"
msgstr "ML 所需乘法因子不可接受"

#: ../../chapters/04-productivity/environmental-productivity-ml-common-reference.md:233
#: d2c91975849f4d9d8041a1145116e887
msgid "Preserve the appraisal record but do not report a finite index"
msgstr "保留评价记录，但不报告有限指数"

#: ../../chapters/04-productivity/environmental-productivity-ml-common-reference.md:279
#: be5106c38e9446e686a6c07646ca4287
msgid ""
"Truncating a valid negative distance to zero removes information and changes"
" the index. Infeasibility, by contrast, means that no solution exists under "
"the maintained joint-production and bad-output constraints. It cannot be "
"repaired by assigning a large or zero distance."
msgstr "把有效负距离截断为 0 会删除信息并改变指数。不可行则意味着在维持的联合生产和非合意产出约束下不存在解，不能用赋予一个很大距离或零距离来修复。"

#: ../../chapters/04-productivity/environmental-productivity-ml-common-reference.md:284
#: 0f67a2fcaa4743328aa0663d7ca11951
msgid ""
"Cross-period infeasibility is often economically informative. A bad-output "
"equality or weak-disposal relation may be unable to reproduce a plan from "
"another year because the observed pollution mix has changed sharply. Before "
"changing the estimator, ask whether pollutant definitions, measurement "
"methods, treatment activities, or the assumed disposal relation changed. If "
"a different environmental technology is substantively justified, all four "
"evaluations should be recomputed under that one coherent production account."
msgstr "跨期不可行往往具有经济信息。由于观测污染组合明显改变，非合意产出等式或弱可处置关系可能无法再现另一年度方案。在更换估计器前，应先询问污染物定义、测量方法、治理活动或所假设处置关系是否改变。如果另一种环境技术在实质上更合理，就应在同一个连贯生产账户下重算四次评价。"

#: ../../chapters/04-productivity/environmental-productivity-ml-common-reference.md:292
#: 1c8696f7e50b4876af44498322d432f1
msgid "One plant transition, with one benchmark sensitivity check"
msgstr "一个工厂转变，以及一项标杆敏感性检查"

#: ../../chapters/04-productivity/environmental-productivity-ml-common-reference.md:294
#: 6633adb4a3cc40e393520168df148906
msgid ""
"The bundled `environmental_panel` follows six electricity producers from "
"2020 to 2023. Inputs are energy and labor, electricity is desirable output, "
"and carbon dioxide is undesirable output. Consider Central between 2020 and "
"2021:"
msgstr ""
"内置 `environmental_panel` 跟踪 2020—2023 年六家发电企业。投入是能源和劳动，电力为合意产出，二氧化碳为非合意产出。考察"
" Central 在 2020—2021 年的变化："

#: ../../chapters/04-productivity/environmental-productivity-ml-common-reference.md:233
#: d702278486d14aaba8e7533eda85f743
msgid "Year"
msgstr "年份"

#: ../../chapters/04-productivity/environmental-productivity-ml-common-reference.md:233
#: c26140b0bf16468f8357933f3a86746c
msgid "Energy"
msgstr "能源"

#: ../../chapters/04-productivity/environmental-productivity-ml-common-reference.md:233
#: 25ee8d3fc19548c292ed9cfbc5820fdc
msgid "Labor"
msgstr "劳动"

#: ../../chapters/04-productivity/environmental-productivity-ml-common-reference.md:233
#: c68d7a37b31546098df993e67806bdc2
msgid "Electricity"
msgstr "电力"

#: ../../chapters/04-productivity/environmental-productivity-ml-common-reference.md:233
#: 6651c477a74440f3a7f95e82345093d3
msgid "CO$_2$"
msgstr "CO$_2$"

#: ../../chapters/04-productivity/environmental-productivity-ml-common-reference.md:233
#: 5c3920fa6e8540c5a9e30bc8df022490
msgid "2020"
msgstr "2020"

#: ../../chapters/04-productivity/environmental-productivity-ml-common-reference.md:233
#: 440b81fdc4bb4f67b7980624a07d1f3b
msgid "110.0"
msgstr "110.0"

#: ../../chapters/04-productivity/environmental-productivity-ml-common-reference.md:233
#: 72ba3ce7ef9f4b2cbc272ccec86de10d
msgid "55.00"
msgstr "55.00"

#: ../../chapters/04-productivity/environmental-productivity-ml-common-reference.md:233
#: b3b9e5d131864386a05deec8d1922a46
msgid "79.376"
msgstr "79.376"

#: ../../chapters/04-productivity/environmental-productivity-ml-common-reference.md:233
#: a4602aad4ab04159a53043058cbd8db0
msgid "285.120"
msgstr "285.120"

#: ../../chapters/04-productivity/environmental-productivity-ml-common-reference.md:233
#: 7aba8771846547e59a0a094ed37a3c95
msgid "2021"
msgstr "2021"

#: ../../chapters/04-productivity/environmental-productivity-ml-common-reference.md:233
#: c75b86ed2c2441c5a8d7895713a5fcbf
msgid "112.2"
msgstr "112.2"

#: ../../chapters/04-productivity/environmental-productivity-ml-common-reference.md:233
#: ad033c2a8130421299063a5985521042
msgid "54.45"
msgstr "54.45"

#: ../../chapters/04-productivity/environmental-productivity-ml-common-reference.md:233
#: 99cc0d7a01674ffb9bbecd1bd8870e8b
msgid "83.742"
msgstr "83.742"

#: ../../chapters/04-productivity/environmental-productivity-ml-common-reference.md:233
#: 96ed9bf706de45c9924c36a90590c7d5
msgid "270.465"
msgstr "270.465"

#: ../../chapters/04-productivity/environmental-productivity-ml-common-reference.md:303
#: a780cb56a8b744a1856e8ce290dbf99d
msgid ""
"Electricity rises and carbon dioxide falls, while the two inputs move in "
"different directions. The index evaluates the complete plan rather than "
"declaring improvement from either raw output change alone."
msgstr "发电量增加、二氧化碳减少，而两项投入朝不同方向变化。指数评价完整方案，不会仅凭任何一项原始产出变化就断言改善。"

#: ../../chapters/04-productivity/environmental-productivity-ml-common-reference.md:307
#: 1b45b596f35e415fba1b97976fb7abc5
msgid "Fit the adjacent-period ML account first:"
msgstr "先拟合相邻期 ML 账户："

#: ../../chapters/04-productivity/environmental-productivity-ml-common-reference.md:338
#: c074b6715caf4e75a82ef36face4b9dc
msgid ""
"The same fitted result provides one screen of every reportable 2020--2021 "
"transition:"
msgstr "同一拟合结果可以筛查所有可报告的 2020—2021 年转变："

#: ../../chapters/04-productivity/environmental-productivity-ml-common-reference.md:233
