msgstr "1.045043"

#: ../../chapters/04-productivity/environmental-productivity-ml-common-reference.md:354
#: b36baac8a34045568d1fc631c4a36785
msgid ""
"Central's contemporaneous operating shortfall is essentially unchanged. "
"Adjacent ML records about 4.51 percent environmental productivity growth. "
"The decomposition places that change in a more favorable opportunity across "
"the two period-specific technologies."
msgstr "Central 的同期经营缺口基本不变。相邻 ML 记录约 4.51% 的环境生产率增长，分解把这一变化归入两个时期特定技术之间更有利的生产机会。"

#: ../../chapters/04-productivity/environmental-productivity-ml-common-reference.md:358
#: fa55d1513e614c2abfd466469989a638
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"The adjacent result also illustrates a valid signed cross-period distance. "
"The underlying comparison is feasible and "
"$D_{2021}^{2020}\\approx-0.004534$, so $1+D_{2021}^{2020}>0$. Central's 2021"
" plan is slightly beyond the opportunity supported by the 2020 reference "
"under the chosen programme. The negative value is retained as part of the "
"period-specific opportunity change."
msgstr ""
"相邻期结果还展示了有效的带符号跨期距离。底层比较可行且 $D_{2021}^{2020}\\approx-0.004534$，所以 "
"$1+D_{2021}^{2020}>0$。在所选方案下，Central 的 2021 年方案略微超出 2020 "
"年参照所支持的生产机会。该负值作为时期特定机会变化的一部分予以保留。"

#: ../../chapters/04-productivity/environmental-productivity-ml-common-reference.md:364
#: a6f5f95451e94f41828ff7c63a0d84c5
msgid ""
"Four available 2020 to 2021 adjacent-period environmental productivity "
"changes are plotted for South, East, Central, and Coastal, while North and "
"West are listed separately because their required cross-period comparisons "
"are infeasible"
msgstr ""
"绘出 South、East、Central 和 Coastal 四个可得的 2020—2021 年相邻期环境生产率变化；North 与 West "
"单列，因为其必要跨期比较不可行"

#: ../../chapters/04-productivity/environmental-productivity-ml-common-reference.md:369
#: 22ac6bdb01bb46dbbf3214b206312791
msgid ""
"Four plants have all four appraisals needed for an adjacent-period "
"comparison. Each point therefore compares operating performance and observed"
" production opportunities under the weak common-factor CRS technology. North"
" and West are listed separately because at least one required cross-period "
"comparison is infeasible. Their absence is not zero productivity change or "
"evidence of poor management. The reported differences remain conditional "
"production comparisons, not causal ratings of management, investment, or "
"regulation."
msgstr ""
"四家工厂拥有相邻期比较所需的全部四次评价，因此每个点都在弱共同因子 CRS 技术下比较经营绩效与观测生产机会。North 和 West "
"因至少一次必要跨期比较不可行而单独列出。未显示不表示生产率变化为零，也不是管理不佳的证据。报告差异仍是条件性生产比较，不是对管理、投资或监管的因果评级。"

#: ../../chapters/04-productivity/environmental-productivity-ml-common-reference.md:378
#: a597d11b85e5407a916e04aa09c17ea5
msgid ""
"The two unavailable transitions have different reference boundaries. North's"
" 2020 plan cannot be represented by the 2021 technology under the maintained"
" production assumptions. For West, neither period's plan can be represented "
"by the other period's technology. Both transitions therefore remain "
"unavailable rather than being turned into zero change or a poor-performance "
"score."
msgstr ""
"两个不可得转变具有不同的参照边界。在维持的生产假设下，North 的 2020 年方案无法由 2021 年技术表示；West "
"的两个时期方案都无法由另一时期技术表示。因此，两项转变都保持不可得，而不会被改成零变化或低绩效得分。"

#: ../../chapters/04-productivity/environmental-productivity-ml-common-reference.md:384
#: 09fc2c2c55ee4f1aaaa9b4d54a395516
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"As a robustness check, the same transition can be re-evaluated against one "
"full-horizon technology, often called GML {cite:p}`oh2010`. This changes the"
" admitted reference information rather than repairing missing adjacent "
"comparisons:"
msgstr ""
"作为稳健性检查，可以把同一转变放到覆盖全时段的一个技术下重新评价，这通常称为 GML "
"{cite:p}`oh2010`。这改变了获准使用的参照信息，而不是修复缺失的相邻期比较："

#: ../../chapters/04-productivity/environmental-productivity-ml-common-reference.md:364
#: 6f5cbe6e26a74f8f9598576dd0c07167
msgid "Reference-information policy"
msgstr "参照信息政策"

#: ../../chapters/04-productivity/environmental-productivity-ml-common-reference.md:364
#: 27f5132b56d34010a42cc89702ddb7f9
msgid "Two contemporaneous technologies"
msgstr "两个同期技术"

#: ../../chapters/04-productivity/environmental-productivity-ml-common-reference.md:364
#: 7f1244ea5cce4912ba9a4dcc296f9c64
msgid "One full-horizon technology"
msgstr "一个覆盖全时段的技术"

#: ../../chapters/04-productivity/environmental-productivity-ml-common-reference.md:364
#: df639b4abb7d465d8b43491ea34ab7a4
msgid "1.004603"
msgstr "1.004603"

#: ../../chapters/04-productivity/environmental-productivity-ml-common-reference.md:401
#: 2af0e54c9d9a4a0e8ca17c2794dd052c
msgid ""
"Central's full-horizon value remains above one but is smaller; it is only a "
"sensitivity result, not a replacement for adjacent-period ML, and it must be"
" recomputed when the admitted information horizon changes."
msgstr "Central 的全时段数值仍大于 1，但更小；它只是一项敏感性结果，不能替代相邻期 ML，而且在获准信息时段变化后必须重新计算。"

#: ../../chapters/04-productivity/environmental-productivity-ml-common-reference.md:405
#: ceed3f4d008941349a92d4e800f58264
msgid ""
"The common benchmark also lets a decision maker ask a direct longer-horizon "
"question. Suppose the plant's transition plan spans 2020 to 2023. A GML "
"endpoint compares those two complete production-and-emissions plans against "
"the same retrospective opportunity set. It does not assume that the annual "
"path was smooth, nor does it identify which investment, operating decision, "
"or regulation produced the change. It simply makes the start and end of the "
"declared management horizon comparable under one fixed information vintage."
msgstr ""
"共同标杆还让决策者能够提出直接的长期问题。假设工厂转变方案覆盖 2020—2023 年，GML "
"端点比较把两个完整生产—排放方案放到同一个回溯性机会集下评价。它不假定年度路径平滑，也不识别哪项投资、经营决策或监管造成变化，只是使既定管理时段的起点和终点在一个固定信息版本下可比。"

#: ../../chapters/04-productivity/environmental-productivity-ml-common-reference.md:413
#: be44ae197bbe40b2b615c50bd97ece9c
msgid ""
"Consecutive reporting remains the default. A study can request every forward"
" pair or name only the horizon it needs:"
msgstr "连续期报告仍是默认选择。研究可以请求所有正序日期对，也可以只指定所需时段："

#: ../../chapters/04-productivity/environmental-productivity-ml-common-reference.md:426
#: c3bf5be394764aa2b26a2097f9abfe2b
msgid ""
"The all-horizon table has $DP(P-1)/2$ rows for $D$ plants and $P$ periods, "
"so its results, diagnostics, and disclosed peers grow quadratically with the"
" number of dates. The production appraisals do not: each plant-period plan "
"needs at most one contemporaneous and one global solve, and those appraisals"
" are reused across horizons. This distinction makes a complete research "
"table computationally disciplined while still too large to treat as a "
"default management display."
msgstr ""
"全时段表对 $D$ 家工厂、$P$ 个时期包含 $DP(P-1)/2$ "
"行，因此结果、诊断和披露参照单元数量随日期数平方增长。生产评价本身不会如此增长：每个工厂—时期方案最多只需一次同期求解和一次全局求解，并在各时段间复用。这使完整研究表在计算上仍有纪律，但规模过大，不适合作为默认管理展示。"

#: ../../chapters/04-productivity/environmental-productivity-ml-common-reference.md:433
#: 28e91f174fbd47ed89c71e863a65387a
msgid ""
"If a plant is absent from one selected date, matching is handled for that "
"pair alone. Dropping the unavailable change does not erase its other "
"observations from the global environmental benchmark. Raising on the "
"mismatch instead forces the researcher to resolve the missing institutional "
"history. In either case, pair selection changes the reported horizons, not "
"the full-sample technology."
msgstr "若工厂在所选某一日期缺失，只对该日期对处理匹配。删除不可得变化不会从全局环境标杆中抹去它的其他观测；因不匹配而报错则迫使研究者处理缺失的机构历史。无论哪种方式，日期对选择只改变报告时段，不改变完整样本技术。"

#: ../../chapters/04-productivity/environmental-productivity-ml-common-reference.md:439
#: 5cddef636f224cd086cdb7388df3e689
msgid "For a figure, fit the one endpoint that the caption will name:"
msgstr "绘图时，只拟合图注所说明的一个端点："

#: ../../chapters/04-productivity/environmental-productivity-ml-common-reference.md:450
#: 10df54eefd5d4039a2a5432154a251a2
msgid ""
"Plotting all pairs under the ending year alone would hide whether each point"
" began in 2020, 2021, or 2022. A reader should never have to infer the base "
"year of an environmental productivity statement from context."
msgstr "若只按结束年份绘制所有日期对，就会掩盖每个点始于 2020、2021 还是 2022 年。读者绝不应从上下文猜测环境生产率陈述的基年。"

#: ../../chapters/04-productivity/environmental-productivity-ml-common-reference.md:454
#: 2a4ff8e3d3f94c95bfb02921a5413c86
msgid ""
"The adjacent interpretation requires four meaningful appraisals that "
"reconstruct the headline change and its two components under one consistent "
"treatment of resources, services, residuals, and reference periods. If a "
"comparison is unavailable or the decomposition does not close, the "
"transition has no defensible productivity statement. Detailed numerical "
"diagnostics are available in the DEAPack Documentation; substantive "
"production assumptions still require economic and institutional "
"justification."
msgstr ""
"相邻期解释要求四次评价都具有实质含义，并且在资源、服务、残余物和参照时期处理一致时，能够重构核心变化及其两个分量。比较不可得或分解不能闭合时，该转变就没有可辩护的生产率陈述。详细数值诊断见"
" DEAPack Documentation；实质生产假设仍需经济与制度依据。"

#: ../../chapters/04-productivity/environmental-productivity-ml-common-reference.md:461
#: 829abab105ef4b95b8513628e49e7ac0
msgid "What should a decision maker be told?"
msgstr "应向决策者说明什么？"

#: ../../chapters/04-productivity/environmental-productivity-ml-common-reference.md:463
#: c458708cc23447ee8a63270b048f0bef
msgid ""
"Adjacent-period ML should be reported only when both neighboring operating "
"environments deserve symmetric standing and all four evaluations are "
"substantively meaningful. A missing cross-period comparison is part of that "
"evidence and must remain visible rather than being replaced with a "
"convenient finite number."
msgstr ""
"只有当两个相邻经营环境都应得到对称地位，且四次评价都具有实质含义时，才应报告相邻期 "
"ML。缺失的跨期比较是证据的一部分，必须保持可见，不能替换为一个方便的有限数值。"

#: ../../chapters/04-productivity/environmental-productivity-ml-common-reference.md:468
#: 1f5de69ee09e4adab386b8f0481e9525
msgid "A defensible report should state:"
msgstr "有根据的报告应说明："

#: ../../chapters/04-productivity/environmental-productivity-ml-common-reference.md:470
#: 451b540988b347d2a108b5fe8ea94263
msgid "which variables are inputs, desirable outputs, and undesirable outputs;"
msgstr "哪些变量是投入、合意产出和非合意产出；"

#: ../../chapters/04-productivity/environmental-productivity-ml-common-reference.md:471
#: b5a06dddb00248e7a0e13c5222f4c9e8
msgid "how joint production and undesirable-output disposability are modeled;"
msgstr "如何建模联合生产与非合意产出可处置性；"

#: ../../chapters/04-productivity/environmental-productivity-ml-common-reference.md:472
#: 95a6f085c6aa4eef99791541b9465a42
msgid "what one unit of the environmental improvement programme means;"
msgstr "一个环境改进方案单位具体表示什么；"

#: ../../chapters/04-productivity/environmental-productivity-ml-common-reference.md:473
#: 7b8a1cbef4ca44a49b0066fb7118e5bf
msgid "which returns-to-scale assumption defines the opportunity set;"
msgstr "哪一项规模报酬假设界定生产机会集；"

#: ../../chapters/04-productivity/environmental-productivity-ml-common-reference.md:474
#: 269f73ec467f42ba80c9cb7c6223503d
msgid "which two annual technologies define the four benchmark evaluations; and"
msgstr "哪两个年度技术界定四次标杆评价；以及"

#: ../../chapters/04-productivity/environmental-productivity-ml-common-reference.md:475
#: 7f01d6e4b5b8438f92f0a364858269ed
msgid ""
"whether negative distances, infeasibilities, or inadmissible factors "
"occurred."
msgstr "是否出现负距离、不可行或不可接受因子。"

#: ../../chapters/04-productivity/environmental-productivity-ml-common-reference.md:477
#: 74c55a6f78804483a6f2d2913cc8fb9b
msgid ""
"Results near one need numerical tolerances and honest recognition of "
"uncertainty in pollution measurement. ML can describe a change in "
"contemporaneous environmental shortfall, a change in best-observed "
"opportunity, or a plan lying beyond another period's technology. Without "
"further evidence, the following remain outside its claim:"
msgstr ""
"接近 1 的结果需要数值容差，也要诚实承认污染测量的不确定性。ML "
"可以描述同期环境缺口变化、最佳观测机会变化，或某方案超出另一时期技术。没有进一步证据时，下列主张都超出其范围："

#: ../../chapters/04-productivity/environmental-productivity-ml-common-reference.md:483
#: bd0e6d460d434f9394c06b0a1fdcce02
msgid ""
"the causal effect of regulation, innovation, investment, ownership, or "
"management;"
msgstr "监管、创新、投资、所有制或管理的因果效应；"

#: ../../chapters/04-productivity/environmental-productivity-ml-common-reference.md:484
#: a6f9690c01ae4bb499433a7df9f84993
msgid ""
"the monetary value of pollution damage, abatement expenditure, profit, or "
"social welfare;"
msgstr "污染损害、治理支出、利润或社会福利的货币价值；"

#: ../../chapters/04-productivity/environmental-productivity-ml-common-reference.md:486
#: 019dcdf05e9a4ae8b4918cb714b38278
msgid ""
"whether the benchmark can be adopted given engineering, finance, demand, and"
" local regulatory constraints;"
msgstr "在工程、财务、需求和地方监管约束下能否采用标杆；"

#: ../../chapters/04-productivity/environmental-productivity-ml-common-reference.md:488
#: 151c63a1deeb412cb04a68f55fe8cc90
msgid "that observed prices or preferences favor the same improvement programme; or"
msgstr "观测价格或偏好是否支持同一改进方案；或"

#: ../../chapters/04-productivity/environmental-productivity-ml-common-reference.md:489
#: bb1ec438a051425b8c2ad33d66515de2
msgid ""
"that another defensible environmental technology or direction would preserve"
" the ranking."
msgstr "另一种有依据的环境技术或方向是否会保持排序。"

#: ../../chapters/04-productivity/environmental-productivity-ml-common-reference.md:492
#: 6e339e612f2e457f8c66e7ab94b9bcc9
msgid ""
"Environmental productivity is a production comparison, not a complete policy"
" evaluation. Once joint production, undesirable-output disposability, and "
"the improvement programme are explicit, adjacent-period ML offers an "
"intelligible view of changing operating performance, best-observed practice,"
" and the evidence behind the benchmark. A causal or welfare evaluation "
"requires a different research design."
msgstr ""
"环境生产率是一项生产比较，不是完整政策评价。只要明确联合生产、非合意产出可处置性和改进方案，相邻期 ML "
"就能清楚展示经营绩效变化、最佳观测实践变化以及标杆背后的证据。因果或福利评价需要另一种研究设计。"

